# XSH thrd_exit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Calling thrd_exit() from a destructor and the exact number of passes
# beyond those a test can rely on are not tested.

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.001
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread that calls thrd_exit(v) (from a function it called) stops
           there: nothing after the call runs, and thrd_join() obtains v
           (tried with 42, -9 and 0).
test       t/001-status.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.002
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       For a key with a destructor and a non-null value, thrd_exit() sets
           the value to null and calls the destructor once with the old
           value: tss_get() in the destructor returns null.
test       t/002-destructor.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.003
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A destructor that sets the key's value again (twice) is called
           again for each new value: three calls in all.
note       NOTINUSE when the destructor iteration limit reported by sysconf()
           is below three.
test       t/003-repeat.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.004
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       When a thread ends with thrd_exit(), a pipe it opened stays open
           in the process and an atexit() routine has not run.
test       t/004-no-process-cleanup.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.005
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A process whose only thread calls thrd_exit(7) exits with status
           0, and its atexit() routines run.
note       The child writes a byte from its atexit routine; the parent waits
           up to 10 s for the child to end, then kills it (FAIL).
test       t/005-last-thread.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_exit.006
anchor     functions/thrd_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A key made by pthread_key_create() with a destructor, holding a
           non-null value in a thread that ends with thrd_exit(), has its
           destructor called once with that value.
test       t/006-pthread-key.c
